This repository is published so that players, auditors and security researchers can read the
code that runs qu-BETICS and check it. It is NOT open source software.

1. What you may do
   a. View and read the source code.
   b. Download it and build or run it on your own computer, only to review it, test its
      security, or check that it matches the software served at betics.io and admin.betics.io.
   c. Quote short parts of it when discussing, reviewing or reporting on it.

2. What you may not do without prior written permission from the copyright holder
   a. Copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense or sell the code or any part of it.
   b. Use the code, or anything derived from it, to run, host or offer any service, website or
      game, whether commercial or not.
   c. Create derivative works based on the code.
   d. Use the qu-BETICS name, logo or other brand assets. They are not licensed by this file.

3. Security research
   Testing on your own computer is welcome. Do not attack, overload or try to access the live
   services, other players' accounts or funds. Report problems privately as described in
   SECURITY.md.

4. Contributions
   If you send an issue, pull request or suggestion, you allow the copyright holder to use it
   freely, without payment or obligation.

5. Third party components
   Third party packages and files keep their own licences (for example the npm dependencies
